+++ b/docs/plans/2026-10-20-m4-viewer.md
@@ -0,0 +1,238 @@
+# M4 plan: full-screen photo viewer (pager, pinch/pan/double-tap, swipe-down close, long-press)
+
+Spec: `docs/specs/2026-10-16-simplification-design.md` §3.1 (build with installed libs), §3.3 (viewer), §3.4 (tests),
+D24 (gallery), D29 *default* (viewer order while open). Features: M4-01 this plan + gesture wiring · M4-02
+`gallery-gestures.ts` · M4-03 route + pager + counter + ✕ + detail tiles open it · M4-04 zoom/pan/close gestures ·
+M4-05 long-press sheet · M4-06 walkthrough · M4-07 review. Each task: RED test first, then code; `check.sh` green
+per commit.
+
+Starting point (after M3): detail renders `PhotoGrid photos={spotPhotos(spot, media)}` with **no** `onPressPhoto`
+(tiles role `image`). gesture-handler 2.32 and reanimated 4.5.1 (+ worklets 0.10.1) installed; before M4-01 only
+`app/_layout.tsx` imported reanimated (side-effect import), nothing imported gesture-handler.
+
+## M4-01 wiring (done in this feature)
+
+- `app/_layout.tsx`: outermost element `<GestureHandlerRootView style={styles.root}>` (`root: { flex: 1 }`) around
+  `ThemeProvider` (so the Stack, every modal and the root `StatusBar` sit inside it).
+- `jest.setup.ts`: `import 'react-native-gesture-handler/jestSetup'` (package's own mocks of its native module,
+  buttons, Pressable) + **new** `jest.mock('react-native-worklets', () => jest.requireActual('react-native-worklets/src/mock'))`.
+  Existing reanimated mock kept as is. Found while wiring: the reanimated mock alone **cannot load** under
+  reanimated 4 (`react-native-reanimated/mock` imports worklets, whose native module throws `loadUnpackers` of
+  undefined in Jest); it never ran before because no tested file imported reanimated. The worklets mock fixes it.
+- `src/__tests__/root-layout.test.tsx` (2 tests): RootLayout (providers reduced to children) renders exactly one
+  `GestureHandlerRootView` with style `{ flex: 1 }` containing the Stack and its screens; a `Gesture.Tap().withTestId`
+  inside a `GestureDetector` is fired via `fireGestureHandler(getByGestureTestId('tap'))` and its `onEnd` runs once.
+  Both fail without the jestSetup import (`RNGestureHandlerModule.default.install is not a function`).
+- iOS export (`npx expo export --platform ios`): exit 0 before and after. Hermes bundle **4,060,375 B before →
+  4,215,187 B after** (+154,812 B ≈ +151 KB: gesture-handler's JS; reanimated was already bundled).
+
+## Route (M4-03)
+
+- File `app/spot/[id]/photos.tsx`; params `id`, `index` (string; `parseInt`, NaN → 0, clamp to `[0, n-1]`, so
+  `'99'` on 7 photos opens at 6).
+- `app/_layout.tsx`: `<Stack.Screen name="spot/[id]/photos" options={{ presentation: 'fullScreenModal', headerShown: false }} />`.
+- Opened from detail: `PhotoGrid onPressPhoto={(i) => router.push({ pathname: '/spot/[id]/photos', params: { id, index: String(i) } })}`
+  (test accepts that or `'/spot/<id>/photos?index=3'`; M4-03 picks the string form if the object form makes the
+  assertion awkward). Tiles become role `imagebutton` (PhotoGrid already does this when `onPressPhoto` is set).
+- Missing spot (`id` not in store) → centred 'Spot not found' (same as detail).
+- Root `View` `flex: 1, backgroundColor: '#000'`; `<StatusBar hidden />` from `expo-status-bar` rendered inside the
+  screen: expo-status-bar stacks props per mounted component, so unmounting restores the root's `style="dark"`
+  bar (no manual restore).
+- Chrome (absolute, over the pager, `useSafeAreaInsets` top): counter `"{page + 1} / {n}"` top-centre (white,
+  `accessibilityRole="text"`, `accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"`); ✕ top-right: `Pressable accessibilityRole="button"
+  accessibilityLabel="Close"`, `hitSlop` so the target is ≥ 44×44, `onPress → router.back()`.
+- Back gesture / Android hardware back: no interception; the Stack pops the modal (spec §3.3 "Back gesture also
+  closes"). `fullScreenModal` on iOS has no edge-swipe, so swipe-down + ✕ are the iOS exits.
+
+## Pager choice: `FlatList` horizontal `pagingEnabled` + `getItemLayout`
+
+Why: spec §10 lets the builder pick FlatList or `Animated.ScrollView`. FlatList gives virtualization (a spot may have
+20 photos; `windowSize={3}`, `initialNumToRender={1}`, `maxToRenderPerBatch={1}` → at most ~3 decoded full-size
+images; M4-03 dropped `removeClippedSubviews`: with horizontal paging + `initialScrollIndex` on iOS it is a known
+source of blank pages, and `windowSize` already bounds decoding), `initialScrollIndex` (needs `getItemLayout`: `(_, i) => ({ length: width, offset:
+width * i, index: i })` with `useWindowDimensions().width`; every page is exactly one window wide, so this is exact),
+and `scrollEnabled` as a plain prop for the zoom lock. `Animated.ScrollView` would render all 20 pages and need manual
+initial offset. RN's `FlatList` (not gesture-handler's): page gestures fail on horizontal movement at 1× (below), so
+the native scroll view wins horizontal swipes without cross-wiring.
+
+- `data`: the viewer's order (D29): ids snapshotted from `spotPhotos(spot, mediaBySpot[id])` on mount (`useState`
+  initialiser), then each render maps them to current `Media` rows and drops removed ones. So 'Set as primary' does
+  not jump the photo to page 1 under the user; the detail grid reorders (primary first) as usual.
+- `keyExtractor` = media id; `showsHorizontalScrollIndicator={false}`.
+- Page index state: `onMomentumScrollEnd` → `Math.round(contentOffset.x / width)`, clamped. Test fires
+  `fireEvent(list, 'momentumScrollEnd', { nativeEvent: { contentOffset: { x: 5 * width, y: 0 } } })` → '6 / 7'.
+- Built in M4-03: the counter shows `min(page, n-1)`. **M4-05 must** keep the page pinned to a photo after a removal
+  (the M4-03 review: removing a photo before the current one, or the last one, leaves the native offset on the old
+  page): track the shown photo's id, and `scrollToIndex({ index, animated: false })` when `n` changes.
+- `scrollEnabled={pagingEnabled(scale)}` where `scale` is React state fed by the current page's `onScaleChange`
+  (M4-04); reset to 1 on page change.
+- Each page: `View` width × height, `accessibilityLabel="Photo N of M"`, `accessibilityHint="Double-tap and hold for
+  options"` (M4-05), containing `ZoomablePhoto`.
+- Image: `expo-image` `<Image source={{ uri: resolvePhotoUri(m.file_path) }} contentFit="contain" recyclingKey={m.id}
+  style={StyleSheet.absoluteFill} />` (recyclingKey: recycled cells never flash the previous photo).
+
+## Gesture composition (M4-04): `src/components/ZoomablePhoto.tsx`
+
+Props: `{ uri: string; recyclingKey: string; width: number; height: number; onScaleChange?: (scale: number) => void;
+onRequestClose?: () => void; onLongPress?: () => void; testIdPrefix?: string }`. Exported from
+`src/components/index.ts`. Target < 150 lines excluding styles.
+
+Shared values (reanimated): `scale`, `savedScale`, `tx`, `ty`, `savedTx`, `savedTy`, `dragY` (swipe-down offset at 1×).
+Every number comes from `gallery-gestures.ts`; worklets read only shared values and props captured as plain numbers
+(`width`, `height`), never React state. Pure functions are marked `'worklet'` so they run on the UI thread.
+
+```ts
+const pinch = Gesture.Pinch()
+  .onUpdate((e) => { scale.value = clampScale(savedScale.value * e.scale); /* focalZoom → tx/ty */ })
+  .onEnd(() => { savedScale.value = scale.value; clamp tx/ty via clampPan; scheduleOnRN(onScaleChange, scale.value) });
+const pan = Gesture.Pan()            // rebuilt (useMemo on `zoomed` boolean state) so its config can change
+  // at 1×: vertical only → the FlatList keeps horizontal swipes
+  .activeOffsetY(zoomed ? undefined : [-10, 10]).failOffsetX(zoomed ? undefined : [-10, 10])
+  .onUpdate((e) => zoomed ? (tx/ty = clampPan({ x: savedTx + e.translationX, y: … }, scale, viewport))
+                          : (dragY.value = Math.max(0, e.translationY)))
+  .onEnd((e) => { if (shouldClose(e.translationY, scale.value)) scheduleOnRN(onRequestClose); else dragY → withTiming(0);
+                  savedTx/savedTy = tx/ty });
+const doubleTap = Gesture.Tap().numberOfTaps(2)
+  .onEnd((e) => { next = toggleZoom(scale.value); scale → withTiming(next); tx/ty → next === 1 ? 0 : clampPan(focalZoom(e, scale, next)); scheduleOnRN(onScaleChange, next) });
+const longPress = Gesture.LongPress().minDuration(450).onStart(() => scheduleOnRN(onLongPress));
+const composed = Gesture.Simultaneous(pinch, pan, Gesture.Exclusive(doubleTap, longPress));
+```
+
+- `scheduleOnRN` from `react-native-worklets` (reanimated 4's replacement for `runOnJS`; both exist in 4.5).
+- `zoomed` (React state, `scale > 1.05` via `pagingEnabled`) is set through `onScaleChange` too; it only rebuilds
+  the pan's activation offsets.
+- Animated style: `transform: [{ translateX: tx }, { translateY: ty + dragY }, { scale }]`; backdrop opacity follows
+  `dragY` (`1 - dragY / 400`, floor 0.4) as visual feedback for the swipe-down.
+- Each gesture `.withTestId(\`${testIdPrefix}-pinch|pan|double-tap|long-press\`)` → tests use
+  `fireGestureHandler(getByGestureTestId('viewer-pan-0'), [{ state: State.BEGAN }, { state: State.ACTIVE, translationY: 150 }, { state: State.END, translationY: 150 }])`
+  (names from `node_modules/react-native-gesture-handler/lib/typescript/jestUtils/jestUtils.d.ts`:
+  `fireGestureHandler`, `getByGestureTestId`). Proven in Jest by `root-layout.test.tsx`.
+- Zoom lock test (M4-04 step 2): `screen.UNSAFE_getByType(ZoomablePhoto)` → `act(() => props.onScaleChange(2))` →
+  FlatList `scrollEnabled` false; at 1× true.
+
+### Built in M4-04 (differs from the sketch above)
+
+- `ZoomablePhoto.tsx` is 143 lines with no styles block, so no fallback to react-native-zoom-toolkit (nothing installed).
+  The long-press gesture and `onLongPress` prop are left to M4-05.
+- Shared values use `.get()` / `.set()`, not `.value`: the React Compiler lint (`react-hooks/immutability`) rejects
+  `.value =` inside `useMemo`.
+- Test ids are `${testIdPrefix}-pinch|pan|double-tap`, and the viewer passes `testIdPrefix="viewer-<page index>"`, e.g.
+  `viewer-2-pan`.
+- The gestures are wrapped by an untransformed page `View`, so focal and tap coordinates are in page space. Only the
+  inner `Animated.View` is transformed.
+- Pinch: `onStart` records `startScale/startTx/startTy` and sets `pinching`. `onEnd` snaps to 1 when
+  `pagingEnabled(scale)`, otherwise keeps the scale, then animates to `clampPan` and reports the scale.
+- Pan has `maxPointers(1)`. `onStart` records `panZoomed = !pagingEnabled(scale)`. A pan that started at 1× only drives
+  `dragY = dragDown(translationY)` (new pure function). A zoomed pan applies the per-frame `changeX/changeY` in
+  `.onChange`, and skips frames while `pinching`, so a pinch starting or ending mid-pan causes no jump (the Opus review's
+  Important finding). The viewer closes only when `success && !panZoomed && shouldClose(dy, scale)`, so a cancelled drag
+  never closes it.
+- The swipe-down backdrop fade is not built: the root is already black, so there is nothing to fade. The photo follows
+  the finger down and springs back.
+- Viewer: `zoom` is React state fed by `onScaleChange`, `scrollEnabled={pagingEnabled(zoom)}`, and it is reset to 1 on
+  `momentumScrollEnd`.
+- Back gesture / Android hardware back: unchanged, no interception. The Stack pops the modal (see Route).
+- `jest.setup.ts`: reanimated's mock `useSharedValue` made a new value every render. It is now wrapped in `useState`,
+  so it is stable like the real one; without that, a gesture spanning a re-render saw 1× again.
+- Jest limits (left for the phone check in M4-06):
+  - `fireGestureHandler` skips activation criteria, so `activeOffsetY/failOffsetX` (the pager keeps horizontal swipes
+    at 1×) is not tested.
+  - Every call starts a new gesture, so a pinch in the middle of a pan cannot be simulated.
+  - The `useAnimatedStyle` mock is evaluated once per render, so transforms are not asserted.
+  - Review Minor 4: while the first pinch from 1× is still running, `scrollEnabled` is still true. If a sideways-drifting
+    pinch pages the list on the phone, the fix is gesture-handler's `FlatList` with `Gesture.Native()` interop.
+
+## Pure functions: `src/utils/gallery-gestures.ts` (M4-02)
+
+All `'worklet'`, no imports from React or reanimated. Constants exported: `MIN_SCALE = 1`, `MAX_SCALE = 4`,
+`DOUBLE_TAP_SCALE = 2.5`, `ZOOMED_EPSILON = 1.05`, `CLOSE_DISTANCE = 120`.
+
+```ts
+type Point = { x: number; y: number };
+type Size = { width: number; height: number };
+clampScale(scale: number): number                              // [1, 4]
+toggleZoom(scale: number): number                              // scale < 1.05 ? 2.5 : 1
+clampPan(t: Point, scale: number, viewport: Size): Point       // |x| ≤ width*(scale-1)/2, |y| ≤ height*(scale-1)/2; scale ≤ 1 → {0,0}
+pagingEnabled(scale: number): boolean                          // scale <= 1.05
+shouldClose(dy: number, scale: number): boolean                // scale <= 1.05 && dy > 120
+focalZoom(focal: Point, scale: number, nextScale: number, viewport: Size, translation: Point = {x:0,y:0}): Point
+                                                               // translation keeping `focal` (view coords) fixed;
+                                                               // focal at the centre → {0,0}
+```
+
+`clampPan` bounds use the viewport, not the image's contained size (spec values: scale 2 on 390×844 → ±195, ±422).
+That lets a letterboxed photo pan its black bars into view when zoomed; accepted for now (simple, testable),
+revisit on the phone. `focalZoom` takes `viewport` (for the centre) in addition to the feature text's
+`(focal, scale, nextScale)`, plus an optional current `translation` (default `{0,0}`) so a pinch that starts
+panned keeps its focal point: `t' = d − (next/scale)·(d − t)`, `d = focal − centre` (M4-02 built it this way;
+the tests always pass `viewport`). `-0` results
+are normalised to `0` so `toEqual({ x: 0, y: 0 })` holds.
+
+## Long-press sheet (M4-05)
+
+- `Alert.alert(title = 'Photo', undefined, [{ text: 'Set as primary', onPress }, { text: 'Remove photo', style:
+  'destructive', onPress }, { text: 'Cancel', style: 'cancel' }])`. On iOS three buttons render as a vertical
+  alert list, close enough to an action sheet. **No `ActionSheetIOS`, no new dependency.**
+- Set as primary → `updateSpot(spotId, { primary_photo_id: media.id })` (`useSpotActions`); counter unchanged (D29
+  keeps the order).
+- Remove photo → `Alert.alert('Remove this photo?', 'It is taken off this spot.', [{ text: 'Cancel', style:
+  'cancel' }, { text: 'Remove', style: 'destructive', onPress }])` (no camera-roll promise: Quick Add photos are
+  never in the camera roll) →
+  `removePhotos([media.id])` (`useMediaActions`; resolves the ids removed). If that photo was the spot's primary
+  (`spot.primary_photo_id === id`, or no explicit primary and it was `primaryPhoto`), `updateSpot(spotId, {
+  primary_photo_id: <the photo now shown in its place, i.e. next in viewer order, else previous> ?? null })`.
+  Remaining 0 → `router.back()`. Page index clamps to the new last page; counter 'N / 6'.
+- The page's `onLongPress` comes from the long-press gesture; the hint text tells VoiceOver users to double-tap and
+  hold, which iOS passes through as a long press.
+
+### Built in M4-05
+
+- `ZoomablePhoto` gains `onLongPress` and a `Gesture.LongPress()` (`<prefix>-long-press`, `minDuration(LONG_PRESS_MS)`),
+  composed as `Simultaneous(pinch, pan, Exclusive(doubleTap, longPress))`. It ignores a long press while `pinching`.
+  `LONG_PRESS_MS = 500` lives in `gallery-gestures.ts`: inside `Exclusive` the long press waits for the double tap to
+  fail, and that happens only after the Tap's 500 ms `maxDuration`, so a shorter value would do nothing. The component
+  is 149 lines (startTx/startTy merged into one `startT` point to stay under 150).
+- Viewer: each page has `accessibilityHint="Double-tap and hold for options"` plus `accessibilityActions` `longpress`
+  ('Photo options') and `onAccessibilityAction`, so TalkBack (which sends a long click, not touches) and the VoiceOver
+  Actions rotor reach the same Alert.
+- The actions take a photo id and read the stores when a button is pressed (`getState()`), not the render's closure.
+  Found by a RED test: after 'Set as primary' on another photo, removing it from a page whose callback had been
+  captured earlier did not see it as primary.
+- The shown photo is pinned by id (`pos = { id, index }`). A removal sets `pos` to the photo now in its place (next,
+  else previous), resets the zoom to 1×, and a `useLayoutEffect` on `count` calls `scrollToIndex({ animated: false })`
+  before paint. That fixes the M4-03 review finding (also for a photo removed before the shown one).
+- Remove order: `removePhotos` → (failed: Alert "This photo couldn't be removed", nothing else) → none left:
+  `router.back()` → if it was the primary (`primaryPhoto`, so an implicit first photo counts too, as in edit):
+  `updateSpot(primary_photo_id: next ?? null)`, not awaited, failure only logged. 'Set as primary' failure: Alert.
+- Not guarded: pressing an option twice quickly runs it twice (Alerts are modal; review Minor 9, left as is).
+- **For M4-06's phone checklist** (Jest's `fireGestureHandler` skips Simultaneous/Exclusive relations): hold two
+  fingers still for ~0.5 s and then pinch: no options Alert; a double tap still zooms and never opens the options;
+  a long press opens them after about half a second; VoiceOver: double-tap and hold opens them, and the Actions rotor
+  lists 'Photo options'.
+
+## Fallback rule (spec §3.1)
+
+If `ZoomablePhoto` cannot stay **under ~150 lines excluding styles** with the composition above, M4-04 may instead
+`npx expo install react-native-zoom-toolkit` (pure JS over gesture-handler + reanimated) in its own `chore:` commit,
+use its `ResumableZoom`/`Gallery`, and must record that here and in the progress log. No other gallery dependency.
+
+## Tests
+
+| Feature | File | Cases |
+|---|---|---|
+| M4-01 | `root-layout.test.tsx` | GestureHandlerRootView flex 1 wraps Stack; jest-utils fires a Tap (done) |
+| M4-02 | `gallery-gestures.test.ts` | clampScale 0.5→1, 6→4, 2.2→2.2; toggleZoom 1→2.5, 2.5→1, 1.04→2.5; clampPan scale 1 → {0,0}; clampPan({500,-900}, 2, 390×844) → {195,-422}; pagingEnabled 1 true, 1.06 false; shouldClose 121/1 true, 119/1 false, 300/2 false; focalZoom centre → {0,0} |
+| M4-03 | `photo-viewer.test.tsx` | index '2' on 7 → '3 / 7'; ✕ role button 'Close' → `router.back`; momentumScrollEnd to page 5 → '6 / 7'; index '99' → '7 / 7'; unknown id → 'Spot not found'; pages labelled 'Photo N of 7'; root bg '#000' |
+| M4-03 | `spot-detail.test.tsx` | press `photo-tile-3` → `router.push` to `/spot/<id>/photos` with index '3' |
+| M4-04 | `photo-viewer.test.tsx` | scrollEnabled true at 1×, false after `onScaleChange(2)`; pinch 2× locks / 0.5 unlocks; pinch ending at 1.04 snaps (reports 1); double tap toggles; pan END dy 150 at 1× → `router.back`, 119 → not, at 2× → not; ZoomablePhoto: clamps to 4, cancelled swipe never closes |
+| M4-04 | `gallery-gestures.test.ts` | dragDown 150→150, −40→0 |
+| M4-05 | `photo-viewer.test.tsx` | long-press page 2 → Alert buttons Set as primary / Remove photo (destructive) / Cancel; Set → `updateSpot(id, { primary_photo_id })`, counter same; Remove → 2nd alert 'Remove this photo?' → `removePhotos([id])` once, 'N / 6'; remove last → `router.back`; remove primary → `primary_photo_id` next id / null; hint text |
+
+Viewer tests mock `useSpotActions`/`useMediaActions` (as edit tests do) and seed the zustand stores; `Alert.alert`
+via `jest.spyOn(Alert, 'alert')`, buttons pressed by calling `mock.calls[0][2][i].onPress()` inside `act`.
+
+## Unresolved questions
+
+1. D29: keep the viewer's order while open after 'Set as primary' (default), or jump the photo to page 1?
+2. `clampPan` uses viewport bounds (letterbox bars can pan into view when zoomed). Fine, or bound by the contained
+   image size (more maths, needs the photo's aspect ratio)?
